Let’s try it. Same festival. Give the audience a different reason to hold its breath.

He walks out. The light is so bright he can only see the first row. His hands are shaking.

“My name is Brandon, and I made this.”

Thunder cracks. Three full seconds early.

From the front row, a kid yells, “Do it again!”

So he does. He gives the thunder guy a big conductor’s windup. This time they both miss the cue. The kid falls sideways laughing, and Brandon has to step away from the mic because now he’s laughing too.

As his eyes adjust, he can see all the way to the back. There’s a guy standing in the shadows with his arms folded, trying very hard to keep a straight face. Brandon points at him.

“Sir, you look like you know when thunder is supposed to happen.”

The guy unfolds his arms. “Whenever the kid says.”

And for the rest of the show, it does.